<title>AUSTRIA: UAE's Rakad sees no market impact of Iraq's return.</title>
<headline>UAE's Rakad sees no market impact of Iraq's return.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC President and acting UAE oil minister Rakad bin Salem bin Rakad said on Tuesday he saw no market impact from the possible return of Iraqi oil exports.</p>
<p>&quot;Practically there is nothing,&quot; Rakad said when asked whether he saw any impact on the market.</p>
<p>&quot;I don't think it will change anything,&quot; he added.  </p>
<p>Rakad was speaking ahead of Wednesday's full OPEC meeting.</p>
<p>The oil ministers of Venezuela, Saudi Arabia, Kuwait, Qatar, Algeria and a delegation from Iraq are expected to arrive here later today for the meeting.</p>
<p>-- Vienna Newsroom +431 713 2034</p>
</text>
